{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) requested creation of differential tests for `cmd/tsort` (topological sort utility) in the go-unix-utils repository. The task is Task ID 5597 on branch `task/generation-run44-5597`. Specifically:\n   - Create `cmd/tsort/tsort_test.go` with differential tests comparing the Go tsort implementation against GNU `gtsort` (Homebrew coreutils)\n   - Cover all requirements from srd102-tsort: R1.1-R1.4 (core sort and I/O) and R2.1-R2.3 (exit codes and SIGPIPE)\n   - Follow the project's differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils`\n   - No git commands allowed — git is managed externally by the orchestrator\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing: running Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, comparing stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` API for test execution\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling the Go binary under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gtsort\")` for finding the reference binary, with `t.Skip` if not found\n   - Graceful skip when `cmd/tsort/main.go` doesn't exist during generation runs\n   - Topological sorting: reads pairs \"A B\" meaning A precedes B, outputs sorted order one per line\n   - Cycle detection with stderr diagnostics\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for all differential tests\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd102-tsort.yaml` — Successfully read. Contains all requirements:\n     - R1.1: Read pairs from stdin/FILE, produce topological ordering on stdout\n     - R1.2: Detect cycles → stderr diagnostic, continue sorting, exit 1\n     - R1.3: Odd number of tokens (in